      "reverseHunks": [
        {
          "afterOffset": 515,
          "afterBytes": 68,
          "beforeText": "\t\t<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"synth.css?v=scsp-fm-self-1\" />\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 17712,
          "afterBytes": 725,
          "beforeText": "\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>In 2OP, Self uses X32/Y0 to average two sound-stack histories. Only one OP can feed itself, and the other OP may receive it. Depth 0 is Off in this Synth adapter. Auto and Code clear that OP's two history cells at a new note; live Depth edits keep history. This initialization is Synth software.</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>This graph editor and its voice allocation are Synth software over SCSP slot modulation. Custom accepts acyclic 2 / 4 / 6OP connections plus this bounded 2OP Self prototype. Two-OP cycles and 4/6OP feedback remain future work; raw physical CH controls keep their existing behavior.</p>\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 18725,
          "afterBytes": 273,
          "beforeText": "\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Switching to 4/6OP removes unsupported Self connections while keeping the other routes and outputs. The zero-delay editor core's steady Self histories are one and two native 44.1 kHz samples old; full physical SCSP pipeline accuracy is not implied.</p>\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 43140,
          "afterBytes": 104,
          "beforeText": "\t\t\t\t\t\ttwo inputs per operator, with one Self-feedback OP in 2OP. General cyclic\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 43696,
          "afterBytes": 72,
          "beforeText": "\t\t<script type=\"module\" src=\"synth.js?v=scsp-fm-self-1\"></script>\n"
        }
      ]
