      "reverseHunks": [
        {
          "afterOffset": 3504,
          "afterBytes": 311,
          "beforeText": "sources per target in Custom4/6. Custom2 keeps one source per target and supports\none self-feedback operator, described below. Two self operators, self plus an\nexternal input at the same target, multi-operator cycles and Custom4/6 self\nfeedback are rejected before changing the current sound. These are software\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 3886,
          "afterBytes": 319,
          "beforeText": "In **Custom2**, select an operator and choose **Self · A/B (2 taps)** for Input X.\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 5519,
          "afterBytes": 244,
          "beforeText": "later editing. Resizing a Custom2 self graph to Custom4/6 removes the self edge\nwhile retaining supported external edges and outputs. A graph left dormant under\na fixed template is projected the same way when Custom is selected at that size;\nthe dormant graph does not enable higher-operator feedback.\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 14056,
          "afterBytes": 403,
          "beforeText": ""
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 15471,
          "afterBytes": 407,
          "beforeText": "A supported Custom2 self graph saves as **version 8**, with its complete graph\nand optional individual depths. This takes precedence over versions 5 or 7.\nOlder versions 1–7 reject self graphs; version 8 requires an actual supported\nself graph. Non-self sounds retain their established v4–v7 formats.\n"
        },
        {
          "afterOffset": 17625,
          "afterBytes": 90,
          "beforeText": "and version 8 for supported Custom2 self-feedback.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
